+/*
+ * Stained Glass OS: ipconfig's and netsh's way to the network settings
+ *
+ * The network settings are NetworkManager's, behind sg-netctl (sg-session),
+ * which decides from the Unix account what the caller may do: anyone with a
+ * session may look, administrators (and SYSTEM, an elevated program) may
+ * change addresses. A Windows program runs it as a native program with a
+ * temporary file as its output (patch 0078 gives it that), and reads the
+ * answer: lines, the last "OK" or "ERROR <kind> <message>".
